.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Next.js
.next

.nx/cache
.nx/workspace-data

vite.config.*.timestamp*
.claude/worktrees
.nx/polygraph
.nx/self-healing
.vercel

# `nx graph --file` dumps: point-in-time artifacts with no reader in the
# repo; a committed one rots into a stale project list (AGL-1834).
/project-graph.json

# `nx migrate` writes this, then `nx migrate --run-migrations` consumes and
# discards it. It is generated, never source. It was committed from 2021
# (600beb395) through 33 nx upgrades because the ignore rule read
# `/.migrations.json` — a leading dot nx never writes, so the rule never
# matched. A committed one is worse than stale: `--run-migrations` defaults
# to this path, so it re-applies migrations already applied (AGL-2486).
/migrations.json

# Transient scratch dir written while uploading to the DAM; never source.
.dam-upload-tmp/

# Monaco's `min/vs`, copied out of node_modules by `apps/console/next.config.js`
# at build time (AGL-1779). ~15 MB / 121 files, and it is generated: committing
# it would rot silently against the `monaco-editor` pin in package.json. The
# copy is not optional — the build FAILS if it cannot be produced, because the
# only alternative is `@monaco-editor/loader`'s jsDelivr default.
/apps/console/public/monaco/

# Next writes these on `next dev` startup — `generate-agent-files.js`, called
# from `app-info-log.js` in the `next` package. Both files carry a
# `BEGIN:nextjs-agent-rules` block telling agents to read the bundled docs
# because this Next version differs from their training data, and `next dev`
# RE-ADDS the block, so deleting them is futile: they came back for every
# agent in this shared checkout, four permanently-untracked files that are
# exactly the condition a `git add -A` accident needs (AGL-2486).
#
# Ignored rather than committed for two reasons. They are generated and
# pinned to one Next version, so a committed copy rots against the pin like
# the Monaco rule above; and `apps/*/CLAUDE.md` is one line, `@AGENTS.md`,
# a Claude Code IMPORT directive — committing it would load Next's guidance
# into every agent's context repo-wide, which is a deliberate decision to
# take on its own, not a side effect of a dependency's dev server.
#
# Listed as four EXACT anchored paths, not `**/AGENTS.md`: these are the only
# two Next apps in the workspace (`apps/console`, `apps/tenant` — the only
# `next.config.js` files), and a hand-written AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md anywhere
# else, including the repo root, stays tracked as normal. Add a third Next
# app and its pair shows up untracked, which is the right moment to decide
# about it rather than have this rule decide silently.
/apps/console/AGENTS.md
/apps/console/CLAUDE.md
/apps/tenant/AGENTS.md
/apps/tenant/CLAUDE.md
